  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">Gesti&#xf3;n Sostenible de la Tierra</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Environment and Livelihoods for a Vital Amazon (SELVA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Ecuador):  .Weak.governance, unsustainable land-use practices, and limited economic.opportunities are driving deforestation and forest degradation in the northern.Ecuadorian Amazon, threatening critical ecosystems and the livelihoods of.Indigenous nations such as the Siona, Siekopai, and Shuar, and local.communities. Illegal activities, including agricultural encroachment, poaching,.and logging, further erode sustainable management of natural resources and.territorial integrity...USAID is.partnering with Indigenous peoples and local communities to protect 213,631.hectares of forest through conservation agreements. The agreements promote.sustainable land-management practices, safeguard forest ecosystems, and deliver.tangible economic benefits. Strengthened governance structures empower.Indigenous leaders and communities to participate in decision-making, enhancing.territorial management and long-term sustainability...USAID will.set up robust territorial monitoring systems and early detection mechanisms,.enabling communities to find and respond to threats. These systems will protect.forests and resources, supporting biodiversity conservation. USAID will enhance.Indigenous governance by strengthening leadership, fostering inclusivity, and.building capacity for managing protected areas. This approach will help.communities coordinate with law enforcement to address illegal activities, and.keep control over their territories...By.integrating conservation, sustainable land use, and governance, USAID&apos;s efforts.will protect critical ecosystems, reduce deforestation, and restore degraded.lands. These actions will advance Ecuador&apos;s National Biodiversity Strategy,.empowering Indigenous nations to secure their territories and improve.livelihoods. These actions will ensure that forests remain vital to the health.of the Amazon and its people...This.mechanism attributes $500,000 towards the Andean Amazon earmark......... ....... .</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="ES">El prop&#xf3;sito de esta actividad es trabajar con las comunidades ind&#xed;genas locales en el paisaje del &#xe1;rea objetivo del norte de la Amazon&#xed;a ecuatoriana para proteger 213,631 hect&#xe1;reas de bosques y participar en pr&#xe1;cticas sostenibles de manejo de la tierra dentro de los territorios ind&#xed;genas, manteniendo reservas de carbono ayudando as&#xed; a Ecuador a cumplir con sus contribuciones determinadas a nivel nacional.</narrative>
  </description>
